Q: How to create proc macro that accesses associated types A: <p>Does a marker trait + blanket impl do the trick for you?</p>
<pre><code>trait T {
    type AT1;
    type AT2;
}

// marker trait
trait T_i32_f64 {}

// blanket impl for all marked types
impl&lt;S: T_i32_f64&gt; T for S {
    type AT1 = i32;
    type AT2 = f64;
}

struct S;

// mark S and imply implementing default types without macro call
impl T_i32_f64 for S {}
</code></pre>
